  "notes": "Cash basis county. Balance sheet (re-check 2026-10-29, user rule 2026-10-27): governmental funds Balance Sheet - Cash Basis (p3, Total column) used because its totals (9,967,888) equal the government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1); fund balance by classification (restricted 424,293 = p1 Restricted; assigned 7,976,726; unassigned 1,566,869). Top-level receipts from governmental funds statement p4 total column; Taxes 7,771,616 split into property and motor vehicle taxes 7,168,449 and inheritance 603,167 using the Statement of Activities (p2); the combined property/MV line cannot be separated further. State 4,574,957 has no printed breakdown (no homestead/pro-rate lines), kept as state aid. Receipts 'Local' (and the Local detail lines) recorded as charges for services/fees: the Statement of Activities (p2) shows charges for services 1,357,677 of the 1,439,611 Local total. Disbursements: 'Debt service' not split into principal/interest (principal and interest combined). Detail: General Fund schedule (pp5-8) and the budget schedule for all other governmental funds (pp9-11) recorded; the nonmajor combining schedule (p12) duplicates the nonmajor lines in pp9-11 and is not recorded to avoid double counting. Object mapping: 'Personnel services' = salaries and wages; 'Operating expenses' (a catch-all object) = not itemized; 'Capital outlay' = equipment purchases; 'Equipment rental' = rent/leases. Printed lines showing '-' for actual are omitted (e.g., Bridge disbursements, Register of Deeds disbursements, Drug Law Enforcement, Opioid Recovery disbursements, Local Assist). General fund transfers out 4,730,000 are in the Miscellaneous department and are recorded as other financing; printed Total Cash Disbursements includes them. General fund transfers receipt budget 610,000 actual 0 omitted. detail_totals for pp9-11 are the per-fund printed totals (Total road, Total transit...); the schedule's grand totals (Total cash receipts 10,122,781 p9, Total Cash Disbursements 9,390,432 p11, both including transfers) span all funds and are not listed separately; single-line funds have no separate total. Read pages 1-12 of 12."
